[Music]  what happened at the end of reacher  season one what does that final scene  mean and what's going to happen in the  show's forthcoming second season keep  watching as we dive right in  for over 20 years readers worldwide have  been enthralled by lead child's book  series about the exploits of  larger-than-life protagonist jack  reacher after 26 novels the character  finally hit the small screen with the  amazon prime original reacher after two  feature films starring tom cruise amazon  studios rebooted the series with alan  richson in the titular role the series  also stars malcolm goodwin as detective  oscar finley and willow fitzgerald is  roscoe the first season runs for eight  episodes and is based on the first novel  of lee child's series killing floor jack  reacher gets off a bus in margrave  georgia only to be arrested immediately  for murder ultimately discovered not to  be involved in the murder he decides to  help with the investigation when more  victims appear including his brother the  small town of margrave is unwelcome to  outsiders including the black lead  detective finley who transferred down  from boston to escape his life in new  england partnered with a young officer  roscoe the trio investigates the murders  continuing to pile up leading them to a  powerful businessman a corrupt federal  agent and even the mayor sitting on the  steps of a gazebo when all is said and  done reacher says he will be moving on  he isn't one to stay rooted in one place  but what did this ending mean and what  is next for reacher  it's just who i am  at the beginning of the season reacher  was ready to leave the murders in  finley's hands and move on but was  forced to stay he only takes on a more  active role in the investigation when he  discovers his brother is a victim  however in the last few moments of the  season a flashback shows reacher and his  brother joe at the bedside of their  dying mother it's revealed that when  they were younger the brothers got into  a fight with a bigger kid joe took the  fall but their mother tells them she  always knew it was jack  he protected a weaker boy because that  was his nature and when reacher ended up  in margrave his mission started his  revenge but along the way his nature led  him to protect someone new the end of  the season sees reacher face the death  of his last family member it's not just  reacher who faces up to his past  throughout the season roscoe also comes  to terms with her legacy during the  season she reveals that the teal family  were rivals of her own family the  conklins in the final minutes of the  warehouse battle she takes out mayor  teal for his part in the criminal  organization and reacher suggests that  she should run for mayor which would  return the town to its rightful place as  we said before finley isn't from  margrave but relocated there to get away  from boston at the beginning of the  season reacher mistakenly pegs the  detective as a divorced man but later  finley reveals he is a widower  in his final scene with reacher he  informs him he is quitting police work  and heads home to move on with his life  reacher isn't a man who likes to stick  around much of his character and story  arc is predicated on him being in a new  place and finding himself in a brand new  form of trouble that means there are 25  more books they could have chosen from  for season two however to stick out as  the best possible options for a  follow-up season since season one began  the jack reacher story on screen with  lee child's first book about the  detective it isn't far-fetched to expect  amazon to next adapt the second book in  the series die trying on the other hand  the series introduces someone from  reacher's past that they can build on  francis neely is a pi and a former  member of reacher's special  investigations unit in the army during  one episode after the pair is attacked  they utter a line which is used in the  summary of the 11th book of the series  bad luck and trouble you do not mess  with the special investigators  of course this could just be  coincidental either way there are dozens  of potential storylines in the novels to  pull from and with alan richton at the  perfect age to keep going amazon could  have a hit series that go on for a  decade or even longer check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  tv shows are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

